    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup faces a challenging slate today, headlined by **Will Smith**, whose score of 65.29 makes him the clear anchor of the day. With a favorable xERA of 4.07 against Roupp and the added value of leading off, **Will Smith** is perfectly positioned to provide multi-category stability. **Masyn Winn** (60.24) and **Brendan Donovan** (59.46) follow as our most reliable secondary options. **Masyn Winn** benefits significantly from a 10% park factor bump that helps negate the moderate hurdle of facing a left-handed starter, while **Brendan Donovan** leverages an elite platoon advantage against the right-handed Burrows to approach the top-tier efficiency threshold.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with the rest of the infield and outfield. **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman** all face the daunting task of squaring off against Sheehan, whose 3.16 xERA is suppressing expectations across the board. While **Jung Hoo Lee** manages a respectable 47.15 score due to his leadoff role and platoon edge, **Matt Chapman** (43.58) and **Gavin Sheets** (41.47) are teetering near our \"Marginal\" cutoff. **Gavin Sheets** is particularly vulnerable; his negative platoon variance against a lefty arm makes him a high-risk start. We opted to bench **Drew Gilbert** (36.02) and **Wenceel Perez** (34.70), both of whom fell beneath our 40.0 floor; **Drew Gilbert** was the closest to inclusion, but his lower-order placement in a tough matchup against Sheehan failed to justify a start over the higher-upside profiles currently in the lineup.\n\nWith **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Geraldo Perdomo** unavailable due to scheduled off-days, our bench depth is strained, leaving little room for error if weather or late lineup shifts impact our core. We are monitoring the situation closely, as the 3.16 xERA assigned to Sheehan represents the primary risk factor for our mid-to-lower tier starters today. We are betting on the volume of our leadoff hitters, specifically **Will Smith** and **Brendan Donovan**, to provide the necessary floor to protect our 5x5 totals while we weather the difficult matchups for **Luis Arraez** and company.",
